---
name: spatial_knowledge
description: >
  One place a persona knows up front, rendered as a Belief in its Knowledge
  (backend/seed.py, seed_spatial_knowledge) and shown in the observation's
  "What you know:" section. Names the place and, when it has known areas, lists
  them; objects within an area are intentionally left out to keep the section
  readable.
inputs:
  place:
    type: string
    description: The place name, e.g. "Hobbs Cafe".
  areas:
    type: string
    description: >
      Comma-joined area names within the place, e.g. "hallway, library". Empty
      when the place has no known areas -- then only the place is named.
sample:
  place: Oak Hill College
  areas: hallway, library
---
{%- if areas -%}
You know {{ place }} — its {{ areas }}.
{%- else -%}
You know {{ place }}.
{%- endif -%}
